== Unipotent subgroups and 2-transitivity

From now on $X$ an irreducible affine variety over $KK$.

#definition[
  An automorphism $g in Aut(X)$ is called _unipotent_ if it is contained in a $GG_a$-subgroup of $Aut(X)$.
  A subgroup $U subset Aut(X)$ is called _unipotent_ if each element of $U$ is unipotent.
]


Algebraic unipotent groups isomorphic to subgroups of unitriangular matrices $U_n (KK) subset GL_n (KK)$.

#fact(title:"(Arzhantsev-Zaidenberg'20)")[
   - The group which acts effectively and  2-transitively on a set of cardinality at least three has trivial center.
   - An algebraic unipotent subgroup $U subset Aut(X)$ cannot act 2-transitively.
]


== Infinite transitivity and flexibility

Let $"SAut"(X)= angle.l GG_a"-subgroups" angle.r subset Aut(X)$

#definition[
  A point $p in X$ is called _flexible_ if the tangent space $T_p X$ is spanned by tangent vectors to $GG_a$-orbits.
  
  A variety $X$ is called _flexible_ if all its smooth points are flexible.
]



#fact(title:"(Arzhantsev-Flenner-Kaliman-Kutzschebauch-Zaidenberg'2013) ")[\
  Let $dim X>=2$. Then the following conditions are equivalent:
  - $"SAut"(X)$ is transitive on the smooth locus $X_"reg"$,
  - $"SAut"(X)$ is  $oo$-transitive on $X_"reg"$,
  - $X$ is flexible.
]
Generalizes to a quasi-affine $X$ and to the open orbit of $"SAut"(X)$.

