== Closedness in $End(X)$
The semigroup of $KK$-endomorphisms $End(X)$ is an ind-variety:
- An affine $KK$-domain $R$ is a union of finite-dimensional $KK$-subspaces.
- If $R$ is generated by $r_1,...,r_k$, then $End(R)$ is closed in $R^k$.

*(Furter--Kraft'18)*
$Aut(X)$ is locally closed in $End(X)$.


