#lemma[
     Let $R=Spec Y$ be an affine domain over $KK$.
   Then the following hold.
- $Jonq_u (k,R)$ is closed in $End(R[x_1,...,x_k])$.
- The map $exp: jonq_u (k,R) -> Jonq_u (k,R)$ is an isomorphism of ind-subvarieties. 
]
#proof[
  (1) We apply the property of closedness of endomorphisms preserving subsets to the set $cal(F)={x_1, dots, x_k}$, letting $S_(x_i) := x_i + R[x_1, dots, x_(i-1)]$.

  (2) Consider a filtration by finite-dimensional subspaces $R[x_1, dots, x_k] = union.big_i R_i$. For each $d>0$, $V_d := xor.big_(i=1)^k (R[x_1, dots, x_(i-1)] inter R_d) partial / (partial x_i)$ is finite-dimensional, as well as the Lie subalgebra $W_d$ generated by $V_d$. Its exponent contains the intersection of $J$ with the $d$-th filtration element of $End(R[x_1, dots, x_k])$. So the ind-structure given by $union.big_i exp(W_i)$ is equivalent to the induced one.
]

