   - $S := (cal(O)(X_h)^times union {0}) inter cal(O)(X)$ is closed in $cal(O)(X)$,
  - $M = {phi | phi(h) in S}subset End(X),$
  - $M = {phi | phi(f) in cal(O)(X) "for all" f in cal(O)(X)} subset End(X_h).$ #qedhere
 ]

#corollary[
  A nested unipotent subgroup $U$ is closed in both $End(X)$ and $Aut(X)$.
]
#proof[
   $L := log U$ is a Lie subalgebra of $jonq_u (k, cal(O)(X)_h^U )$ for some $k>0$ and\ $h in ker L$.  The following inclusions are closed:
   - $L subset jonq_u (k, cal(O)(X)_h)=> U subset Jonq_u (k, cal(O)(X)_h) subset End(X_h)$,
   - $U subset End(X) inter End(X_h) subset End(X)$,
   - $U subset Aut(X)$ since $Aut(X)$ is locally closed in $End(X)$. #qedhere
]


